      "path": "agent/internal/judge/judge.go",
      "summary": "Owns the judge: its command, prompt, answer validation, stamp identity and the stand rule.",
      "annotations": [
        {
          "newRange": [
            31,
            41
          ],
          "summary": "MinConfidence sets 0.55 as the lowest confidence at which a full judgment stands.",
          "rationale": "In the experiment's 300 judgments every right full had 0.55 or more and the two wrong ones (an injected note) had 0.5 and 0.3, so the gate removes the measured false greens without false reds. A 0.7 gate would have turned 8 right Opus answers into false reds. Verified by TestOnlyAConfidentFullJudgmentGoesGreen and a mutation to 0, which fails it. Untested: injections that the model answers with high confidence.",
          "author": "fm/verilex-intent-meaning-check"
        },
        {
          "newRange": [
            146,
            161
          ],
          "summary": "Request escapes the intent's angle brackets and ampersands and wraps it in one pair of request tags.",
          "rationale": "The intent is untrusted data, so it must not close the tag and pose as a rule. TestRequestReachesTheJudgeAsData proves one tag pair and the escaped text reach the judge; removing the escaping fails it.",
          "author": "fm/verilex-intent-meaning-check"
        },
        {
          "newRange": [
            260,
            275
          ],
          "summary": "holds reuses a full judgment while its named claims are unchanged, and a partial or none only while the whole catalog is unchanged.",
          "rationale": "No other claim can make a full's claims prove less, but a new or changed claim may prove what a partial or none missed. TestJudgmentIsReusedUntilItsStampDrifts covers both branches.",
          "author": "fm/verilex-intent-meaning-check"
        },
        {
          "newRange": [
            100,
            122
          ],
          "summary": "Resolve makes a --judge path absolute before it checks, stamps and runs the file.",
          "rationale": "The judge runs from an empty directory, so a relative path failed to start, and a bare name ran a PATH program whose answer was stored under the checked file's identity (S1 of the zero-trust review). TestJudgePathIsTheLaunchersFile failed before the change (relative inconclusive, bare name green on the trap) and passes after.",
          "author": "fm/verilex-intent-meaning-check"
        },
        {
          "newRange": [
            43,
            44
          ],
          "summary": "Format version 2 prevents earlier permissive or whitespace-collapsed judgments from being reused.",
          "rationale": "An old stored answer can violate the new boundary even when its text looks unchanged, so the stamp format invalidates every earlier identity.",
