      "summary": "Owns the judgments store: create-only files named by content digest, read back without trust.",
      "annotations": [
        {
          "newRange": [
            49,
            100
          ],
          "summary": "Find returns only judgments that match their digest, key and claim fingerprints, choosing the most cautious when several hold.",
          "rationale": "The store may be shared between machines and written concurrently, so a damaged or racing file must never turn a result green. The damaged-file step of TestJudgmentIsReusedUntilItsStampDrifts re-judges. Anyone with write access can still forge a judgment; the brain's sandbox hides the store.",
          "author": "fm/verilex-intent-meaning-check"
        },
        {
          "newRange": [
            31,
            43
          ],
          "summary": "DefaultDir returns an error when neither XDG_STATE_HOME nor HOME is set.",
          "rationale": "Without HOME it used to build a relative path, so the store landed in the working directory. Run refuses only intent runs with this error, which TestOnlyAnIntentNeedsTheJudgmentStore checks.",
          "author": "fm/verilex-intent-meaning-check"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
